  "question": {
    "text": "Let the angle $\\theta, 0 \\lt \\theta \\lt \\frac{\\pi}{2}$ between two unit vectors $\\hat{\\mathrm{a}}$ and $\\hat{\\mathrm{b}}$ be $\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{9}\\right)$. If the vector $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}=3 \\hat{\\mathrm{a}}+6 \\hat{\\mathrm{~b}}+9(\\hat{\\mathrm{a}} \\times \\hat{\\mathrm{b}}),$ then the value of $9(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}} \\cdot \\hat{\\mathrm{a}})-3(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}} \\cdot \\hat{\\mathrm{b}})$ is",
    "image": null
