  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}=3 \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}+6 \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{~b}}+9(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}) \\\\\n& \\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{9}\\right) \\Rightarrow \\sin \\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{9} \\Rightarrow \\cos \\theta=\\frac{4}{9} \\\\\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=3|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}|^2+6 \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=3+\\frac{6 \\cdot 4}{9}=\\frac{51}{9} \\\\\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}} \\cdot \\vec{a}=3 \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{~b}}+6|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{~b}}|^2=\\frac{3 \\cdot 4}{9}+6=\\frac{22}{3} \\\\\n& \\therefore 9(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}})-3(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}} \\cdot \\vec{b})=51-22=29<br/>\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
